# The build context for platform.Dockerfile, and nothing else.
#
# BuildKit reads "<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore" in preference to a root .dockerignore,
# so this scopes the filter to this one image instead of claiming a repository-root file
# every future image build would share.
#
# An allowlist, and that is the whole design. The repository root is several gigabytes --
# .claude is worktrees and tool output, .venv, .reference and .mypy_cache are hundreds of
# megabytes each -- and a denylist would have to name each of those and would silently
# ship the next large directory somebody adds.
#
# Two entries more than session.Dockerfile.dockerignore, and both are the migration
# runner: hatchling packages src/managed_agent only, so alembic.ini and migrations/ reach
# the image as files rather than through the wheel.
#
# src/** and migrations/** rather than src and migrations: the pattern must match the
# files inside the directory, not only the directory entry.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!src/**
!alembic.ini
!migrations/**
